  "title": "Tree gadgets of the open knots have bounded hubs",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "For every tree gadget of a non-windable knot, in particular of the six open knots, every axis u and every terminal i: F(u)F(u-bar) <= s_u + F(u + e_i)F(u-bar) + F(u)F(u-bar + e_i), by mapping each linked pair injectively through a one-sided flip of terminal i's arm along the tree route to the first branching knot; so tree gadgets have hub ratio at most 3, and they do exceed 1 (a stored eight-knot tree reaches 12/11). In a gadget with a cycle the arm is not determined: a stored seven-knot gadget with a double edge has two linked pairs with the same image. The inequality for all gadgets is left open as a conjecture, holding on 48,000 random axis-terminal cases and all 336 annealed gadgets of ticket B.",
